                  to Trevélez, the highest village in the Sierra Nevada,
                  renowned throughout Spain for its traditionally cured Serrano
                  ham. From here, we continue to the breathtaking Poqueira
                  Gorge, home to three of the region's most picturesque and
                  authentic white villages: Capileira, Bubión, and Pampaneira.
                  Our stop is the beautiful white village of Capileira, where
                  you'll have time to wander through its narrow, winding
                  streets, browse the local craft shops for souvenirs, and enjoy
                  a coffee on one of the village's charming terraces. We then
                  continue through La Taha, one of the most authentic areas of
                  the Alpujarras, where a collection of tiny traditional white
                  villages is connected by quiet mountain roads and scenic
                  trails. This peaceful and unspoilt landscape offers a fitting
                  finale to our journey around the Sierra Nevada. Our ride
                  concludes at a panoramic viewpoint, where we'll celebrate the
                  successful completion of all five stages with a well-deserved
                  toast while taking in the breathtaking views. Afterwards, a
                  transfer takes us back to our hotel in Níguelas, where our
                  adventure around the Sierra Nevada comes full circle.
